g" medium="image"><media:credit>Jordan Vonderhaar for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>The case involving SpaceX dates back to a letter eight employees wrote and circulated within the company in 2022.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>Jensen Huang Said to Have Had Relationship With Nvidia Executive Who Reports to Him</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-affair.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-affair.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/technology/jensen-huang-nvidia-affair.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>Mr. Huang, Nvidia’s chief executive, is already facing scrutiny over an affair with a Chinese businesswoman who U.S. intelligence determined was a Chinese spy.</description><dc:creator>Ryan Mac, Tripp Mickle and Georgia Gee</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:55:36 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">NVIDIA</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Jen-Hsun Huang</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Jensen Huang</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computer Chip</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Adultery</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Ethics Misconduct Malfeasance</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Spying and Intelligence Agencies</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/11/multimedia/00Biz-Huang-Relationship-wlgb/00Biz-Huang-Relationship-wlgb-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Manuel Orbegozo for The New York Times</media:credit><media:description>Nvidia’s chief executive, Jensen Huang, at the company’s annual conference in San Jose, Calif., in March.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>Nvidia’s Board Is Weighing Jensen Huang’s Future</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/technology/nvidia-jensen-huang.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/technology/nvidia-jensen-huang.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/11/technology/nvidia-jensen-huang.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>Mr. Huang has been under scrutiny for an affair with a woman said to be a Chinese spy, as well as for a relationship with an executive at his A.I. chip company.</description><dc:creator>Tripp Mickle and Maggie Haberman</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:43:00 GMT</pubDate><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computers and the Internet</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Tech Industry</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Board of directors</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Artificial intelligence</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Computer Chip</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Adultery</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">NVIDIA</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Wachtell</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Lipton</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Rosen &amp; Katz</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Jen-Hsun Hu